    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nanimate\n\n### Description\n\nSee actual behavior section. 🎥 \n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Setup `mini.animate`(I'm using lazy.nvim)\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n\tvim.fn.system({\r\n\t\t\"git\",\r\n\t\t\"clone\",\r\n\t\t\"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n\t\t\"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n\t\t\"--branch=stable\",\r\n\t\tlazypath,\r\n\t})\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.animate\",\r\n\t\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\t\tlocal animate = require(\"mini.animate\")\r\n\t\t\tanimate.setup({\r\n\t\t\t\tcursor = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tpath = animate.gen_path.line({\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tpredicate = function()\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t}),\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t})\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Prepare file includes CJK languages like\r\n\r\n```\r\n# Cursor ~\r\n\r\nThis animation is triggered for each movement of cursor inside same windowand buffer.\r\nIts visualization step consists from placing single extmark (see|extmarks|) at certain position.\r\nThis extmark contains single space and is highlighted with `MiniAnimateCursor` highlight group.\r\n\r\n# カーソル\r\n\r\nこのアニメーションは、同じウィンドウとバッファ内でカーソルが移動するたびにトリガーされる。\r\nその視覚化のステップは、1つのエクストマーク(|extmarks|を参照)を特定の位置に置くことから始まります。\r\nこのエクストマークは1つのスペースを含み`MiniAnimateCursor`ハイライトグループでハイライトされます。\r\n```\r\n\r\n3. Move cursor on CJK line and move around\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nText rendering is not corrupted.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/6259812/eb228885-6f7d-4691-88c3-da271b8a3d29\r\n\r\nThis can be reproduced with WezTerm and also Terminal.app.",
